open_app + long_press, the two missing control primitives. open_app uses 'monkey -p <pkg> -c android.intent.category.LAUNCHER 1' (launcher intent) rather than 'am start' so the caller needn't know the activity name; it error-checks 'No activities found'/'aborted'. Rationale: the vision spike proved icon-tapping is the unreliable step (0-1/5 on in-house models), so launching apps by package sidesteps it entirely. long_press = 'input swipe x y x y ms' (hold in place). Built to mirror tap/swipe/key exactly - one-liner core methods, uniform route handlers, shim tools, CLI subcommands. Live-tested on the emulator: open-app launched Settings (process confirmed running + in recent tasks) though it sat behind fahreza's secure PIN keyguard (adb can't bypass a PIN - expected); long-press returned ok. Builds green with --features android.
